    <p>Every new launch in the west now has the same headline: <em>AI</em>. Budget 2026 put artificial intelligence at the centre of Singapore&rsquo;s growth plans, and one-north sits closest to the action. So it&rsquo;s fair to ask whether &ldquo;near the AI hub&rdquo; is a real reason to buy, or just this year&rsquo;s version of &ldquo;near the CBD&rdquo;.</p>

    <p>Here&rsquo;s what we think matters more. Hudson Place&rsquo;s land at Media Circle was won in 2025 at <strong>$1,037 psf ppr</strong> (per square foot per plot ratio &mdash; the land cost per square foot of buildable floor area). In March 2026, the Dover Drive site a short drive away drew a top bid of <strong>$1,556 psf ppr</strong>. That is a gap of <strong>~$519 psf ppr</strong>. Land cost is the biggest input into a developer&rsquo;s selling price, so later launches nearby will most likely have to price higher.</p>

    <p>That is the real story: not a promise of AI-fuelled gains, but an earlier entry price in a precinct the government has already earmarked for thousands of new homes and jobs. It comes with two honest trade-offs &mdash; the MRT walk and the school picture &mdash; which we set out plainly below.</p>

    <p>Below we walk through the five angles you&rsquo;ll hear from every agent presenting Hudson Place, then put it through the <a href="/blog/primekey-analysis-introduction">NAVIS PrimeKey Analysis</a> &mdash; the 8-pillar framework we use to grade any Singapore project on data, not on hype.</p>

    <h2>Quick project facts</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Developer:</strong> Media Circle Alpha Development Pte Ltd &mdash; a joint venture of Qingjian Realty, Forsea Holdings, CYZ Land and Jianan Capital</li>
      <li><strong>Tenure:</strong> 99-year leasehold (from 13 March 2025; ~98 years remaining)</li>
      <li><strong>Total units:</strong> 327 residential units in 2 blocks (Block 20: 23 storeys; Block 18: 15 storeys), plus ~400&nbsp;sqm of shops at level 1</li>
      <li><strong>Land area:</strong> ~7,630&nbsp;sqm (82,129&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft)</li>
      <li><strong>District:</strong> D5 &mdash; Queenstown planning area (Rest of Central Region, RCR)</li>
      <li><strong>Land cost:</strong> $1,037 psf ppr</li>
      <li><strong>Address:</strong> 18 &amp; 20 Media Circle (S139818 / S139819)</li>
      <li><strong>Nearest MRT:</strong> one-north (CC23, Circle Line) &mdash; ~18-minute walk (~4 minutes by bicycle per the developer); Buona Vista interchange (East-West / Circle Line) one stop away</li>
      <li><strong>Schools (1&nbsp;km):</strong> New Town Primary (~0.84&nbsp;km) is the only one, and it has no Primary 1 intake, so there is no 1&nbsp;km ballot advantage. Tanglin Trust School (international) ~5 minutes&rsquo; walk; Fairfield Methodist Primary and ACS (Independent) ~6 minutes by bicycle</li>
      <li><strong>Car park:</strong> 134 lots including 4 commercial (~130 residential lots for 327 units, about 40%), plus 57 bicycle lots and 7 motorcycle lots</li>
      <li><strong>Expected vacant possession:</strong> 30 September 2029</li>
      <li><strong>Sale status:</strong> Now open for sale &middot; average ~$2,499 psf</li>
    </ul>

