    <p>Two-bedders make up <strong>56%</strong> of the project (183 of 327). That tells you who the developer expects to buy: tenants-in-mind investors and young professionals more than large families.</p>

    <h2>The 5 selling angles you&rsquo;ll hear</h2>

    <p><strong>1. &ldquo;Live where the AI economy is being built.&rdquo;</strong> one-north is home to over 50,000 knowledge workers, and Kampong AI &mdash; Singapore&rsquo;s first integrated AI park and live-work community &mdash; is slated for around 2028.</p>

    <p><strong>2. &ldquo;You&rsquo;re buying before the land price reset.&rdquo;</strong> Hudson Place&rsquo;s $1,037 psf ppr land cost is ~$519 psf ppr below the Dover Drive GLS (Government Land Sales) site&rsquo;s $1,556 psf ppr.</p>

    <p><strong>3. &ldquo;Rental demand is built in.&rdquo;</strong> Only around 1,000 private homes exist inside one-north today. Recent median rents nearby include $4,200&ndash;$5,500 for a 2-bedder (Normanton Park, One-North Eden, One-North Residences).</p>

    <p><strong>4. &ldquo;Resort living with a retail podium.&rdquo;</strong> Facilities include a 50&nbsp;m main pool, a second pool, two clubhouses and a tennis court, with shops at level 1. The developer says the shops are common property, so their rent helps offset maintenance fees.</p>

    <p><strong>5. &ldquo;New Queenstown, not just one-north.&rdquo;</strong> The site sits next to the Rail Corridor, with the upcoming Queensway community node (2027) and Holland Village both within easy reach.</p>

    <p>All five are fair points. The question is how much each one should weigh for <em>your</em> household.</p>

    <h2>The honest review &mdash; NAVIS PrimeKey Analysis</h2>

    <p>NAVIS PrimeKey scores a project on eight pillars, each out of 5 stars: MRT connectivity, growth hotspots, the GLS and en-bloc pipeline nearby, project size, remaining tenure, rental yield, school effect, and the MOP cluster (nearby HDB flats reaching their Minimum Occupation Period, a key source of upgrader buyers). It&rsquo;s a shortlisting tool. It tells you where a project is strong and where you need to ask harder questions.</p>

