    <h3>Where Hudson Place scores full marks (5&#9733;)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Growth Hotspots (5&#9733;).</strong> Sits directly inside the one-north / Mediapolis growth area, with zero distance to the hotspot boundary.</li>
      <li><strong>GLS / En-bloc Pipeline (5&#9733;).</strong> Seven confirmed or reserve GLS and en-bloc sites within 2&nbsp;km, including Dover Drive, Slim Barracks Rise (Parcel A), Lyndenwoods, Penrith and Terra Hill. Newer sites set higher benchmark prices &mdash; they also add competing supply.</li>
      <li><strong>Remaining Tenure (5&#9733;).</strong> ~98 years left on the 99-year lease.</li>
      <li><strong>Rental Yield (5&#9733;).</strong> Average 3.6% for the RCR, at the 3.5% threshold for full marks.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where it holds its own (3&ndash;4&#9733;)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Project Size (4&#9733;).</strong> 327 units: big enough for resale liquidity and shared facility costs, small enough to avoid a glut of identical units at resale.</li>
      <li><strong>MOP Cluster (4&#9733;).</strong> 1,718 HDB units within 2&nbsp;km have reached or will soon reach MOP, mainly SkyTerrace @ Dawson (758 units) and SkyVille @ Dawson (960 units). A solid upgrader pool &mdash; though both reached MOP in December 2019, so many of those owners may already have moved.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where it doesn&rsquo;t (1&ndash;2&#9733;)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>MRT Connectivity (1&#9733;).</strong> About an 18-minute walk to one-north MRT (CC23), past the 14-minute threshold for a higher rating. The developer puts it at 4 minutes by bicycle and is applying for a 1-year free shuttle to one-north and Buona Vista MRT (subject to authority approval). Either way, this is not a sub-10-minute walk. Time the route yourself before you commit.</li>
      <li><strong>School Effect (1&#9733;).</strong> The only primary school within 1&nbsp;km, New Town Primary (~0.84&nbsp;km), has no Primary 1 intake, and there is no elite or popular-tier school within 1&nbsp;km. Remember that 1&nbsp;km only gives ballot priority, never a guaranteed place.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What else to weigh (not scored by PrimeKey)</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Parking is tight by design.</strong> About 130 residential lots for 327 homes. one-north is planned as a car-lite precinct, which suits tenants and young professionals, but a two-car family should ask about season parking before booking.</li>
      <li><strong>Supply is coming.</strong> URA plans around 11,000 new homes across Mediapolis and the surrounding areas over the next 10&ndash;15 years. That brings amenities, and it also brings competition for tenants and resale buyers.</li>
      <li><strong>Developer track record in Singapore.</strong> Qingjian Realty has completed around 20 projects here; Forsea is a newer name locally. Ask to see the finishes in a completed Qingjian project, not just the showflat.</li>
    </ul>

