    <h2>Who is Hudson Place Residences actually for?</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>The one-north professional.</strong> You work at Fusionopolis, Biopolis, Mediapolis or NUS and want to walk or cycle to work. The MRT walk matters less when your office is closer than the station.</li>
      <li><strong>The rental-minded investor.</strong> A 2-bedder of 646&ndash;689&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft in a precinct with a large, well-paid workforce and little private stock today. You&rsquo;re buying on land cost and a 5&ndash;10 year view, and you&rsquo;ve priced in the competing supply.</li>
      <li><strong>The upgrader who values space and facilities over a school address.</strong> A 3- or 4-bedder for a household whose children are past the Primary 1 ballot, or who are planning around international schools such as Tanglin Trust nearby.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Who it doesn&rsquo;t suit:</strong> families whose plan hinges on a popular primary school within 1&nbsp;km, households who need a short covered walk to the MRT every day, and two-car families. If one of those describes you, there are launches that will serve you better, and we&rsquo;re happy to show you the comparison.</p>

